# still takes the full reconvert. Each single-identified current sheet
# batch (patch 318's "SHEETID single") now also asks, of the one sheet
# that changed, how much of the document the edit reached, and logs it.
# The numbers are the gate for piece C (multi-root rebuild): C is built
# only if bounded batches dominate on real sites.
#
#  - css.c: per <style> entry, two record tables (B.3): reach_prev (the
#    version the boxes were built from) and reach_cur (the live version),
#    captured in html_css_process_modified_style before the old handle is
#    released. A record is one style rule (group at-rule preludes
#    prefixed; other at-rules and at-statements one record each), hashed
#    FNV-1a over its text with comments blanked and whitespace collapsed.
#    The first edit of a <style> scans the outgoing sheet's source
#    (content_get_source_data); later edits hand reach_cur on. The
#    incoming table is built eagerly from the element's DOM text (B.3's
#    lazy build-at-flush is left to C). <link> sheets keep no table.
#  - html_css_sheet_reach_census(): the common prefix/suffix of the two
#    hash sequences is trimmed; the middle (old + new) is the changed set
#    K (B.2). Unbounded, first cause in this order: no table (no-source),
#    K > 64 (too-many), a changed at-rule/statement (at-rule), counter
#    keywords (counter), a nested block (nesting), a backslash in the
#    prelude (escape), a selector with no anchor (unanchored). Otherwise
#    the anchors (B.1: the rightmost compound with a plain #id/.class,
#    outside functional pseudos, that is the subject or followed by a
#    descendant/child step; id beats class) are resolved in one document
#    walk (B.4: id exact, class through dom_element_has_class, a matched
#    element's subtree skipped). No roots is bounded; a root that is
#    <html>/<body>/<li>, a child of <ol>/<ul>/<menu>, or has no box is
#    declined (B.5's static checks: admission).
#  - macos9_reconvert.c: "LIFE SHEETREACH bounded changed=K anchors=A
#    roots=R walked=N" or "LIFE SHEETREACH unbounded reason=<cause>" beside
#    each "LIFE SHEETID single"; the navigation reset prints "LIFE
